oorly positioned on e2, and Qf2+ forces it to move to d1 or f1, both of which weaken White’s coordination. The check prevents White from developing safely and allows Black to follow up with Nc5 or Rh8-h5, increasing pressure. This move maximizes activity and capitalizes on the king’s vulnerability.\n\nAnswer: Q: h4-f2'}
