\n1 |KWF1|    |    |    |    |    |    |    | 1\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: a7-a5, P: a7-a6, P: b7-b5, P: b7-b6, P: c4-c3, K: c8-b8, K: c8-c7, K: c8-d7, R: d8-d7, R: d8-d6, R: d8-d5, R: d8-d4, R: d8-d3, R: d8-d2, R: d8-d1, R: d8-e8, R: d8-f8, P: g4-g3, B: g5-f4, B: g5-e3, B: g5-d2, B: g5-c1, B: g5-h4, B: g5-f6, B: g5-e7, B: g5-h6, R: g8-f8, R: g8-e8, R: g8-g7, R: g8-g6, R: g8-h8]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Situation: I am playing as Black, and my king is on c8, still in the corner with limited activity. White’s king is exposed on a1, deep in the corner but not yet castled (though castling rights are likely lost due to movement). White has a pawn on e4 and another on h6, both potentially dangerous, but my pieces have active potential. My bishop on g5 is well-placed, eyeing the long diagonal toward the white king. Several pawns are mobile, and rooks on d8 and g8 are ready to act. However, my position is somewhat passive overall, and I need to increase pressure before White consolidates.\n\nEvaluation:\n- **P: a7-a5 / a7-a6 / b7-b5 / b7-b6**: Pushing pawns on the queenside is slow and doesn’t contribute to immediate threats. These moves don’t exploit White’s exposed king.\n- **K: c8-b8 / c8-c7 / c8-d7**: Moving the king early is risky unless necessary. No immediate danger, so king movement is premature.\n- **R: d8-d7/d6/etc. or R: g8-f8/e8/h8/g7/g6**: Lifting rooks could be useful later, but without targets, they lack impact. Rook to f8 might support g-file pressure, but no open file yet.\n- **P: c4-c3**: A pawn push that could