o escort the pawn.\n\nKing move b7-c6 is particularly strong as it heads toward d5 and possibly c5 to support a4 and a3 later. But among the options, b7-a6 directly supports the a5 pawn and prepares a4 with king protection.\n\nReason: The best plan is to push the a-pawn while supporting it with the king. The move K: b7-a6 brings the king to support the advance of the a-pawn, preparing to defend it when it advances. This increases winning chances by coordinating king and pawn to promote. Passive king moves waste time.\n\nAnswer: K: b7-a6'}
