ols central area, good opposition setup\n- K: d6-c6 — lateral shift, neutral\n- K: d6-c7 — retreats\n- K: d6-d7 — retreats vertically\n- K: d6-e7 — retreats diagonally backward\n\nBest choice: **K: d6-c5** — this takes space toward queenside, prepares to mirror or oppose White’s king movements, maximizes king activity, and avoids being pushed back.\n\nIt also minimizes the distance to potential future central control if other pieces existed (though none do), but in pure king endgames, staying centralized and avoiding edges is best.\n\nReason: Moving to c5 centralizes the king slightly and maintains maximum flexibility while obeying adjacency constraints. It avoids passive retreat and keeps balanced positioning.\n\nAnswer: K: d6-c5'}
